  <details class="dc-architecture__section">
    <summary>{{ 'Engineering review: inventory, gaps, and cleanup candidates'|t }}</summary>
    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3 mt-3">
  <section class="dc-architecture__section" id="module-inventory">
    <h3>{{ 'Module inventory'|t }}</h3>
    <p>{{ 'The reviewed repository snapshot contained 2,855 tracked paths. The root defines the Drupal module and links to subsystem designs. Source, configuration, content, and local tooling serve different purposes:'|t }}</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>src/</code>, <code>config/</code> &mdash; {{ 'Server services, controllers, command and access boundaries, schemas, and defaults.'|t }}</li>
      <li><code>js/</code>, <code>css/</code>, <code>templates/</code> &mdash; {{ 'The game and editor browser interfaces.'|t }}</li>
      <li><code>content/</code>, <code>images/</code>, <code>characters/</code>, <code>screenshots/</code> &mdash; {{ 'Bundled content, input examples, and reference assets.'|t }}</li>
      <li><code>tests/</code>, <code>scripts/</code>, <code>tools/</code> &mdash; {{ 'Checks, deployment and QA support, imports, and migration utilities.'|t }}</li>
      <li><code>docs/</code>, <code>.github/</code>, <code>tmp/</code> &mdash; {{ 'Design and contributor guidance, issue templates, and retained analysis artifacts.'|t }}</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="dc-architecture__section" id="future-state">
    <h3>{{ 'Future state and gaps'|t }}</h3>
    <p>{{ 'These are review findings and proposed exit checks, not features already shipped.'|t }}</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>{{ 'Actions across UI, chat, and automation'|t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'The channels have distinct ingress and state paths. Trace each action to its validator, executor, and mutation receipt, then converge on one authoritative executor per action. Verify that replay or duplicate delivery does not apply it twice.'|t }}</dd>
      <dt>{{ 'One authority for an actor’s current room'|t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'Authored starting location, campaign actor location, runtime room, and encounter position represent different or overlapping facts. Establish one live room writer and confirm movement, escort, and reconnect cannot disagree or reset an actor.'|t }}</dd>
      <dt>{{ 'Placement and movement agree'|t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'The terrain passability helper does not inspect placed objects, while the editor and map represent object blocking. Verify normal and forced movement against one occupancy rule, including ports and obstacles.'|t }}</dd>
      <dt>{{ 'Published dungeon authority'|t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'Storyline room binding still reads canonical dungeon row data. Reconcile existing sites without published versions, then validate against the published contract without disrupting supported campaigns.'|t }}</dd>
      <dt>{{ 'Resumable authoring and observable operations'|t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'Extend revision-safe saved work from Storyline to Dungeon and Room. Distinguish model budget failures from invalid tool calls, and verify that revision reporting and backup restores cover both database rows and stored media.'|t }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="dc-architecture__section" id="retirement-candidates">
    <h3>{{ 'Cleanup candidates'|t }}</h3>
    <p>{{ 'These paths are flagged for review, not approved for deletion.'|t }}</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>{{ 'Strong candidates:'|t }}</strong> <code>.phpunit.result.cache</code>, <code>hexmap:review</code> {{ '(missing entry file), superseded reports such as the old Pathbuilder analysis, and adjacent-product documentation under'|t }} <code>docs/jobhunter/</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>{{ 'Check consumers first:'|t }}</strong> <code>js/hexmap-entry.js</code>, <code>src/Service/ActionProcessor.php</code>, <code>scripts/systemd/</code>, {{ 'and tracked analysis artifacts under'|t }} <code>tmp/</code>. {{ 'Preserve active reads, tests, and audit evidence.'|t }}</li>
      <li><strong>{{ 'Retain:'|t }}</strong> {{ 'Shared map components, actor-authority checks, module conversion tools, and compatibility adapters with known callers.'|t }}</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="dc-architecture__section">
    <summary>{{ 'Live Feature Index (HQ Sync)'|t }}</summary>
    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table class="dc-architecture__table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Feature ID'|t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Status'|t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Priority'|t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Release'|t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Acceptance Criteria'|t }}</th>
            <th scope="col">{{ 'Implementation Notes'|t }}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for feature in feature_index %}
            <tr>
              <td>{{ feature.feature_id }}</td>
              <td>{{ feature.status }}</td>
              <td>{{ feature.priority }}</td>
              <td>{{ feature.release }}</td>
              <td>{{ feature.acceptance }}</td>
              <td>{{ feature.implementation }}</td>
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
